#### Setup.

We evaluate on Graph-Land (Bazhenov et al., [2025](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2605.31500#bib.bib257 "GraphLand: evaluating graph machine learning models on diverse industrial data")), a benchmark suite with diverse graph structures, and on ogbn-arxiv and ogbn-products from Open Graph Benchmark (Hu et al., [2021](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2605.31500#bib.bib295 "Open graph benchmark: datasets for machine learning on graphs")), and on standard citation networks (Cora, Citeseer, Pubmed) for compatibility with prior work (Yang et al., [2016](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2605.31500#bib.bib34 "Revisiting semi-supervised learning with graph embeddings")). All experiments use full-batch configuration on a single NVIDIA A100 80GB SXM4. We benchmark GCN for SpMM-based layers, min\min-aggregation for reduction-based layers; for Attention-based layers, we focus on Graph Transformer and GATv2, which has been shown to be more expressive than the original GAT, while our optimization techniques remain broadly applicable to the latter architecture as well.

